// NimbusOS policy for unattended-upgrades (docs/PLAN.md NOTE-34).
//
// Shipped by the nimbusos-release package and read after Debian's
// 50unattended-upgrades. Debian's default also installs regular point-release
// updates automatically; NimbusOS installs only Debian security updates
// automatically. Other Debian updates are offered by "Install updates" in the
// Control Center and by Discover. NimbusOS's own packages are handled by
// nimbus-update (policy Automatic / Notify only / Off), not by
// unattended-upgrades, because unattended-upgrades won't pull in new
// dependencies from outside its allowed origins.
//
// "#clear" empties the list Debian's file built up before the new entries
// are added.
#clear Unattended-Upgrade::Origins-Pattern;
Unattended-Upgrade::Origins-Pattern {
        "origin=Debian,codename=${distro_codename},label=Debian-Security";
        "origin=Debian,codename=${distro_codename}-security,label=Debian-Security";
};

// Never restart the machine on its own; the Control Center shows a
// "Restart now" banner instead.
Unattended-Upgrade::Automatic-Reboot "false";
